;; Cyclic clusters of the module graph: which modules are tangled together, and under what name.
;; Every cluster is a strongly connected component, so no cut short of breaking the cycle removes a
;; module from one. A cluster keeps its name while it shrinks and splits.
;;
;; The :mode key is the switch. Under :observe, CI prints how the clusters changed and fails nothing,
;; and the shrink workflow records the new structure, growth included, with `./bin/mage fix-module-cycles`.
;; Under :enforce, membership is a ceiling: a module joining a cluster, two clusters merging, or a new
;; cycle fails, and the fixer only records improvements, so growth is a hand edit whose PR says why.
{:mode :observe
 :uses
 {api-routes-knot
  #{api-routes
    cloud-migration
    core.cmd}
  foundation
  #{analytics.internal-stats
    api
    app-db
    auth-provider
    events
    models
    parameters.schema
    premium-features
    settings
    task
    tracing}
